# Commit Safety Convention

Every commit message MUST include a one-line stability footer so anyone (including AI agents in future sessions) knows at a glance whether it is safe to reset to.

## Format

```
<type>: <short summary>

<body explaining what and why>

STABLE: <one sentence confirming what works and is safe to revert to>
```

## Stability Footer Examples

```
STABLE: DX11 games (No I'm not a Human, PEAK, Super Battle Golf) launch and play correctly. Safe to revert here if future D3D12/GPTK work breaks DX11.
```

```
STABLE: Bootstrap, auth, and Steam DRM confirmed working on v3.0.0-engine. Clean revert point before refactoring game install flow.
```

```
STABLE: Known broken — intentional WIP. Do NOT treat as a safe revert point.
```

## Rules

- Every commit gets a `STABLE:` line — even WIP commits (just mark them explicitly broken).
- The footer describes **what has been user-confirmed working**, so the next session knows exactly what regression risk exists if they revert here.
- One branch is fine for a feature. Stable commits within it are the safety net.
